    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **50 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI made the `householdId` deterministic and reworked how `sharesHousehold` and duplicate detection behave.\n\n**Core change \u2014 deterministic household id** (`OwnerHousehold.java`)\n- `id(lastName, postcode)` now returns the first 12 hex characters of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)`. Removed the old address-based `sameHousehold` matching.\n\n**Always stamp the id** (`AssignHousehold.java`)\n- Now unconditionally stamps `owner.setHouseholdId(OwnerHousehold.id(lastName, postcode))` \u2014 no repository scan, no back-fill, no dependence on `sharesHousehold`. Owners with the same last name + postcode converge automatically.\n\n**New household-duplicate block** (`CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique.java` + `HouseholdDuplicateException` + handler + escalation YAML)\n- Rejects a create (409) when an existing owner shares the computed `householdId`, **unless** the request set `sharesHousehold`, which bypasses the block so the owner is created as a declared member.\n- Wired into `owners.POST.yml` right after `assignHousehold` and before `checkIdentityUnique`.\n\n**Identity check unchanged in spirit** (`CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` / `OwnerIdentity`)\n- Still compares the full `telephone|email|householdId` key and is **not** bypassed by `sharesHousehold` \u2014 so a full duplicate that also declares `sharesHousehold` (same telephone \u2192 same key) still collides (Cp28).\n\n**Declared members aren't flagged** (`AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`)\n- Returns early with `possibleDuplicate=false` when `sharesHousehold` is set \u2014 a declared household member is not a suspected duplicate.\n\n**Docs** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 updated the `householdId` and `sharesHousehold` descriptions to match the new deterministic, always-present semantics.\n\nThe behavior now matches every checkpoint: same lastName+postcode \u2192 shared id (Cp11/Cp36); second such owner \u2192 409 unless `sharesHousehold` (Cp10/Cp35); declared member created and not flagged (Cp35); household membership drives size while `membershipLevel` stays formula-based (Cp23); full-identity duplicates still 409 (Cp03/Cp25/Cp28).",
